      "math_academy_id": "q-103386",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Mark is mowing the lawn. He wants to determine how much area he can mow as time goes on. What are appropriate units for Mark's purpose, in terms of base units?",
      "worked_solution": "We *measure the change* in the area, as *we change* the time. Consequently, any appropriate unit must take the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{unit of area}}{\\text{unit of time}}.\n$$\n\nThe base unit for area is ${\\text{m}}^{2},$ and the base unit for time is $\\text{s}.$ Therefore, the appropriate units are\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{m}}^{2}}{\\text{s}},\n$$\n\nor, square meters per second.",
